From 372e3f5be365708c247c83f450795415757d654a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandeep Gupta <sandeep.gupta12@ibm.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:40:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] DLM: fix concurrent MigrationState patch races blocking
 same-cluster migration

Three fixes for Decentralized Live Migration (DLM) on same-cluster,
different-namespace topology (ppc64le and all architectures):

1. decentralized.go: guard SourcePersistentStatePVCName against empty string
   Setting PersistentStatePVCName = &"" serialises as an empty non-null
   pointer which the OpenAPI validator rejects (HTTP 422). Only set it when
   the PVC name is non-empty. Affects any VM without PVC-backed storage
   (e.g. container-disk VMs on ppc64le).

2. migration.go: replace whole-object test+replace with per-field patches
   patchVMI() was issuing a single test+replace on the entire
   /status/migrationState object. The sync controller concurrently writes
   sub-fields (sourceState.syncAddress) while virt-controller writes others
   (sourceState.nodeSelectors). Any concurrent write causes the test to fail
   with HTTP 422, permanently blocking SourceState from being written and
   stalling DLM at Scheduling indefinitely. Per-field patches are independent
   so concurrent writes to different fields never conflict.

3. migration.go + synchronization-controller.go: drop test precondition from
   per-field patchMigrationStateField replace operations
   Even after decomposing into per-field patches, each field still used
   test+replace when orig != zero. If the other controller has already
   advanced that field since our informer cache snapshot, the test fails with
   HTTP 422. Since the field is confirmed to exist (orig != zero) and we only
   update its value (no structural change), plain replace is safe and cannot
   fail due to concurrent sibling-field writes.

These fixes also include (from origin/cross-compile):
- syncSourceStateDirect / syncTargetStateDirect: in-process fast path for
  same-cluster DLM avoiding reflexive gRPC self-dial loop
- patchVMIConditions: drop test precondition on conditions array replace
- patchSourceStateFields / patchTargetStateFields: per-sub-field decomposition
  of sourceState and targetState instead of treating them as opaque blobs

