MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In a same-cluster DLM setup, SyncTargetMigrationStatus and
SyncSourceMigrationStatus were silently dropping updates whenever the VMI's
MigrationUID didn't exactly match the incoming migration's UID:

  if MigrationUID != "" && MigrationUID != migration.UID { return success }

This is too strict for DLM.  In same-cluster migrations the source VMI's
MigrationUID is written independently by virt-controller
(updateVMIMigrationSourceWithPodInfo / handleTargetPodHandoff) and can
transiently differ from migration.UID because:

  1. The per-field patch fix (Bug 4/5/6) may not have run yet.
  2. findSourceMigrationFromMigrationID may resolve to a VMIM whose UID
     doesn't exactly match the VMI's cached MigrationUID due to ordering.
  3. A previous run left a stale MigrationUID on the VMI that no longer
     has a corresponding VMIM in cache.

Fix: replace the hard equality check with isActiveMigrationUID().  Only
reject the update if the mismatching UID belongs to a *different, active
(non-final)* migration.  If the VMIM is absent from cache or already final
the UID is stale / from a previous run and it is safe to proceed.

Also update unit tests to reflect the new semantics:
  - stale UID (not in cache) → update proceeds
  - active conflicting migration → update blocked
---
 .../synchronization-controller.go             |  62 +++++--
 .../synchronization-controller_test.go        | 152 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 192 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/synchronization-controller/synchronization-controller.go b/pkg/synchronization-controller/synchronization-controller.go
index 0cf787aaa4..291b3f4162 100644
--- a/pkg/synchronization-controller/synchronization-controller.go
+++ b/pkg/synchronization-controller/synchronization-controller.go
@@ -1025,6 +1025,26 @@ func (s *SynchronizationController) getMigrationIDFromUID(migrationUID types.UID
 	return migrationID, nil
 }
 
+// isActiveMigrationUID returns (true, nil) when the given UID resolves to a
+// migration that exists in the informer cache AND is not yet in a final state.
+// Returns (false, nil) if the migration no longer exists (deleted/evicted) or
+// is already final — both cases mean the UID is stale and safe to ignore.
+func (s *SynchronizationController) isActiveMigrationUID(migrationUID types.UID) (bool, error) {
+	objs, err := s.migrationInformer.GetIndexer().ByIndex(controller.ByMigrationUIDIndex, string(migrationUID))
+	if err != nil {
+		return false, err
+	}
+	if len(objs) == 0 {
+		// Migration no longer in cache — treat as stale/completed.
+		return false, nil
+	}
+	migration, ok := objs[0].(*virtv1.VirtualMachineInstanceMigration)
+	if !ok {
+		return false, fmt.Errorf("found unknown object in migration cache for UID %s", migrationUID)
+	}
+	return !migration.IsFinal(), nil
